## 8. AOP / @Transactional / interceptors / filters

- `@Transactional`: only on the service methods (`ClinicServiceImpl` — `findAllOwners` is `readOnly=true` at line 66; `saveOwner` at line 233). The controller `addOwner` is not transactional, so the multiple `saveOwner` calls are independent transactions.
- AOP aspect: `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java`, lines 37-95. `@Aspect` + JMX `@ManagedResource`. Its around advice pointcut is `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")` (line 77) — it wraps beans annotated `@Repository` to count calls and accumulate timing. Under the active `spring-data-jpa` profile the repository proxy is not a `@Repository`-annotated class, so (as the class Javadoc at lines 30-31 notes) this aspect effectively only joins on the JPA/JDBC impls, not Spring Data JPA.
- Security filter chain: `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`, lines 18-43. `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)`, HTTP Basic, CSRF disabled, all requests authenticated — but the whole config is `@ConditionalOnProperty(name = "petclinic.security.enable", havingValue = "true")` (line 20) and that property is `false` (application.properties:49), so no auth/`@PreAuthorize` enforcement by default. `@CrossOrigin` on the controller (line 52) adds CORS handling. No custom `Filter`/`HandlerInterceptor` beans exist.

